  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and Rationale\n\n**Central Idea**: We target the fundamental bottleneck in minimizing the maximum overlap: **spatial discreteness** and **equilibrium between concentrated peaks** and **uniform coverage**. The solution leverages **higher-resolution periodic patterns**\u2014inspired by theoretical limits in additive combinatorics\u2014to achieve lower C\u2085 values than the base solution. The method creates a *weighted mixture of periodic impulses* that balances high energy concentration with minimal overlap across shifts.\n\n**Why this helps**: Existing methods treat overlap minimization as a local optimization problem, potentially missing global structures. Our construction tightly couples amplitude and phase through a *periodized power spectrum*, ensuring broader feature optimization. This approach reveals that optimal configurations resemble *delta-correlated random fields* constrained to [0,1], leveraging recent discoveries about periodic energy distribution limitations.\n\n**Key Limitations & Challenges**:\n- Requires handling of multi-periodicity across scales\n- May produce candidates with boundary artifacts (needs rejection-based validation)\n- Sensitive to phase initialization but robust under multiple runs\n\n\"The plan specifies default parameters derived from theoretical asymptotics. While local minima exist, our construction's dual frequency nature ensures thresholds are beaten by converging to periodic optima.\"\n\n### 2. Mathspecification\n\n**Representation**: Piecewise-constant function $h(x)$ approximated by $n$ samples $h[i]$ on $[0,2]$\n\n**Variables**: $h[i] \\in \\mathbb{R}, 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1$\n\n**Objective**:\n$$\\min_{h} \\max_{k=-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\Bigg| \\int_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))  dx \\Bigg|$$\nfor integer shifts $k$, measured discretely via convolution.\n\n**Constraints**:\n1. $0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1, \\forall i$\n2. $\\sum_{i} h[i] \\frac{2}{n} = 1 \\iff \\sum_{i} h[i] = \\frac{n}{2}$\n\n**Parametrization**: Use Fourier series truncation at $N_{\\text{freq}}$ terms to enforce statistical regularity. Let $h(x) = \\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\\text{freq}}} a_j \\cdot \\sin(2\\pi j x)$ for $x \\in [0,0.5]$, and repeat periodic boundary.\n\n**Critical Insight**: The Fourier transform of the autocorrelation $\\hat{S}(\\omega)$ shows optimization is equivalent to setting $\\hat{S}(\\omega) \\propto |\\omega|$ for the optimal spectrum.\n\n### 3. Implementation Procedure\n\n**Steps**:\na) **Period Detection & Index Transformation**  \n   - Define: $I_{\\text{max}} = \\round{\\sqrt{n}}$  \n   - Compute fundamental harmonic $k_{\\text{freq}} = \\floor{\\sqrt{n}}$\n\n$b) **HarmonicGenerate**($n, N_{\\text{freq}}$, $\\alpha=1.3$, $\\beta=0.8$):\n   - Ensure $n$ is even\n   - Initialize coefficients $a_j \\sim \\mathcal{U}(0.7,0.9)$ for $j=1$ to $N_{\\text{freq}}$, clipped\n   - Apply frequency tapering: $a_j = a_j \\cdot \\exp(-(j/N_{\\text{freq}})^{0.5})$\n   - Normalize $\\sum a_j = \\alpha$ while retaining intervals\n   - Project to [0,1] via soft clipping: $\\exp(a_j)/(\\sum \\exp(a_j))$\n\nc) **OverlapEstimate**($h$, $n$):\n   - Compute convolution via FFT\n   - Find peak using Simpson's rule\n   - Return max(peak, $\\beta \\cdot \\max_j\\mathbb{E}[a_j])$\n\nd) **ParRefine**($h$, $n$, $\\tau=0.0005$):\n   - Use $m = \\round{\\log_2(n)} \\times I_{\\text{max}}$ phase iterations\n   - L-BFGS-B on projected space with bound tightening\n   - Early termination if improvement < $\\tau$\n\ne) Run **ParGenerate** and **ParRefine** with $n \\in \\{2048, 4096, \\dots\\}$ until $n/2 > 10^6$ samples\n  \nf) Post-filter out candidates scoring > initial record\n\n### 4. Search Choices and Adaptations\n\n**Multi-scale Tuning**:\n- Additive noise generation: $h \\leftarrow h + c \\cdot \\mathcal{N}(0, I)$ for $c=0.002$\n- Spectral clipping: Remove modes $\\lambda < 0.4\\lambda_{\\text{max}}$\n- Early termination threshold $\\tau$ sweep across $\\{1e-5, 1e-6, 0\\}$\n\n**Parametric Variations**:\n1. Turn-off normalization (use true unbounded projection)\n2. Use different frequency scaling: $k_{\\text{freq}} = \\floor{n^{0.55}}$\n3. Alternate between sine+cosine basis\n4. Include $a_0$ constant term with $p=0.02$\n\nEach variant run independently if time remains.\n\n### 5. Budget and Control\n\n**Core Operations Cost Model**:\n1. **Candidate Generation**: $\\Theta(N_{\\text{freq}}^2)$ via FFTs\n2. **Optimization**: $\\Theta(n)$ per L-BFGS-B step\n3. **Resolution checks**: Max $n \\approx \\floor{\\sqrt{\\text{budget}}}$\n\n**Scheduling**:\n- Primary resolution block: 30% computational budget\n- Adaptive restarting: Every $\\floor{\\sqrt{\\text{budget}}}$ samples\n- Fast fallback projection if time under 500s: Linear interpolation + greedy balancing\n\n**Termination**:\n   Return immediately if time under 100s  \n   Return parent solution if under 300s  \n   Return best-known if over 500s\n\n### 6. Validation & Acceptance\n\n**Required Checks**:\na) Project candidate to unity using:\n```python\ndef project_to_unity(x):\n    target = len(x) // 2\n    x = x / (np.sum(x) / target)\n    return np.clip(x, 0, 1)\n```\n\nb) Verify overlap integral < current record via:\n```python\nfrom scipy.signal import convolve\n\ndef compute_overlap_exact(h):\n    n = len(h)\n    d = 1/n\n    corr = convolve(h, 1-h, mode='same')\n    corr[150] # diagnostic point\n    return (0.99*max(corr) + 0.01*sum(corr)).item()\n```\n\nc) Reject candidates showing boundary-boosted correlations  \nd) Acceptance criteria: $C_5 \\leq \\min(\\text{record}, \\text{current}*\\ 0.99)$",
